    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d212">

                <pb facs="0611" n="561" xml:id="pg561"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf. 184.011102/310</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Albert Halstead to the Secretary of
                        State</hi><anchor n="24" xml:id="d212-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 36</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-08-12">August 12, 1919</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Subject: Desire of the German-Austrians for American as
                    president of Reparations Commission.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform the Department
                    that it has been represented to me by persons of influence in Austria that the
                    interests of this small republic would be regarded as better safeguarded if an
                    American citizen were to be elected as President of the Reparations Commission
                    for which the proposed treaty of St. Germain makes provision. In the period
                    since the war in which I have served in Vienna the belief in the sincerity and
                    unselfishness of the American people has been on many occasions strikingly
                    emphasized. The tendency has been to look toward the United States as the only
                    nation without selfish interests or schemes who could possibly assist a stricken
                    people in the hour of their need.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Albert Halstead</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d212-f1" n="24" type="source" xml:id="d212-f1-content">
                <p>Copy transmitted to the Commission by Mr. Halstead under covering letter No. 388,
                    August 12; received August 14.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
